== Noodle Mixture ==

Using a #high speed blender{}, add @Water{3%cups}(filtered) and add the @Egg Yolk Powder{3%Tbsp}, @Lupin Bean Flour{2%Tbsp}(optional), @Sea Salt{1/2%tsp}, @Xanthan Gum{1/2%tsp}, @Sodium Alginate{2%Tbsp}, and @Turmeric{1/4 - 1/2%tsp} into the container and blend on low speed.

Increase to high speed and blend well until thoroughly mixed and mixture is thickened (about ~{3%minutes}).

Add mixture into a #squeeze bottle{}.

== Calcium Bath ==

In a #large bowl{}, add in the @Water{7%cups} and @Calcium Lactate{1%Tbsp} and mix until dissolved and clear.

Squeeze the mixture into the calcium bath while stirring the calcium bath in one direction and noodles will form.

> At this time, the inside of the noodles have not yet set.

Leave the noodles in the calcium bath refrigerated overnight.

== Softening the Noodles ==

When ready to use, remove the noodles from the calcium bath and transfer to a #bowl{}.

To soften the noodles, add @Water{3%cups}(hot tap) to a bowl with the noodles, then add the @Baking Soda{1%Tbsp} and @Lemon Juice{2%Tbsp}.

> There will be a chemical reaction.

Wait ~{6-10%minutes} depending on how the temperature of the hot water.

Soften the noodles as desired, rinse a few times, and discard the water.

Noodle is now ready to be used as spaghetti noodles or egg noodles.